  "sectorConvention": "Indian food-delivery/quick-commerce platforms (Swiggy, Eternal) are valued by SOTP. Food delivery, now EBITDA-positive, is the anchor and gets an EV/adj. EBITDA multiple on FY28E (or Jun/Dec-28) EBITDA. Post-Q2FY27 that multiple ranges 30-40x: Anand Rathi 30x, MOSL 32x, Elara 34x, JM 35x, Nomura 40x, HSIE 40x (Aug), with Swiggy FD typically ~10-15% below Eternal's FD multiple. Quick commerce (Instamart) is where brokers diverge: (a) zero value (JM, Nomura; cash also excluded); (b) a small EV/NOV or EV/GOV multiple (Elara 0.2x NOV; HSIE 0.5x NOV pre-Q2; JM earlier 0.25-0.5x GOV); or (c) a DCF that currently yields ~zero or negative value (MOSL -Rs5/sh at 12.5% WACC/4.5% TG). Minor segments (out-of-home, supply chain, platform innovations) are put at ~0.5-1x EV/Sales or EV/GOV. Net cash is added at full value (HSIE, Elara), haircut (MOSL 0.5x), or ignored (JM, Nomura). A minority (ICICI Securities, three-stage DCF; UBS historically DCF + SOTP) value the whole company on DCF.",
  "notes": "Primary PDFs were read for MOSL, Elara, ICICI Securities, HSIE (Aug-26, pre-Q2) and the Kotak one-pager (Jul-26, pre-Q2). The other SOTP details come from press reports. Methods/multiples were not found for Citi, HSBC, Macquarie, BofA, Goldman Sachs, UBS, CLSA, Nirmal Bang, Nuvama, Bernstein, JPMorgan or Ambit, so those are null. Jefferies is confirmed SOTP-based (TP 435->330), with FD multiples cut, but the numbers were not found. Attribution conflict: one secondary summary placed the '40x FY28 FD EBITDA, zero QC and cash' description after Citi, but Inc42 explicitly attributes it to Nomura, and CNBC-TV18 confirms Nomura ascribes no positive QC value. It is recorded under Nomura only. CLSA's rating is reported as Outperform (Inc42, Jagran) and as Accumulate (Business Today). Goldman's rating is reported as 'Equalweight', which is not Goldman's usual nomenclature, so treat it as unverified. One aggregator claimed Nirmal Bang values FD at 32x FY28E, which looks like a mix-up with MOSL and was not used. In MOSL's SOTP the 'other businesses' line prints INR 146bn but only Rs19/sh, which does not reconcile with FD's INR 605bn = Rs237/sh. Values are recorded as printed, and the per-share column sums to 278 ≈ 280. JM history: Jan-2026 Dec-26 TP 400 (Instamart 0.25x EV/GOV, OOH 1x EV/GOV); Jun/Jul-2026 Reduce, Mar-27 TP 270 (FD 38x FY28 adj. EBITDA, OOH 25x, Instamart/cash zero) and Jun-27 TP 250 (35x); now 200. The JM Oct-26 basis year was not stated. Kotak's Feb-2025 initiation used FD 51x FY27E EV/EBITDA + QC 0.8x FY27E EV/Sales (FV 500). Its current (Jul-26) FV 370 components were not disclosed. Morgan Stanley: Jun-2025 initiation OW 405 at 25x FY28 adj. EBITDA for FD. Jan-2026 reports conflict (EW 375 vs other figures), and no current MS TP was found. BofA's prior Underperform 325 dates to Mar-2025. It is now Neutral 245. Business Today reports the street range as JM 200 (low) to Nuvama 403 (high)."
